===============================GS Message Center message types===============================Modification History: 7-Feb-91 Dave Lyons	Initial Release24-Feb-91 Dave Lyons	Added message #6 for Event Manager.21-Oct-92 Dave Lyons	Noted long-standing use of type $88 by Network Start.			Added $11, $B002.=============================================================================Here is a list of statically-assigned Mesage Center message types.When convenient, use MessageByName instead--but if you want a static number,update this file so everybody knows what you're using.Third parties should use MessageByName; we don't generally assign thesenumbers.  (MessageByName dynamically finds a message type $8000 to $FFFF.)=============================================================================0001  = Finder: Pascal-string pathnames to open or print0002  = Window Manager: desktop pattern/picture (5.0)0003  = Finder front-window message0004  = reserved for Menu Manager (fall-down checking broken--don't use)0005  = used by Scrambler & maybe other CDAs, for toolbox vector chaining0006  = used by Event Manager for default mouse position (6.0)0007  = used by SetStart (Greg Branche)0011  = Finder: GS/OS string pathnames to Open or Print (6.0)0023  = QuickDraw: FastFont handle (the first 2 bytes are a signature)0024  = used by Video Overlay toolset (decimal 36)0044  = AppleShare control panel: MySrvrMessID0046  = AppleShare control panel: MyVolMessID0088  = used by GS.OS:NetBoot:Start:Start.aii8000+ = Used by MessageByName (msg begins with Pascal-string name)        NEVER USE A STATIC MESSAGE TYPE IN THE RANGE 8000..FFFFB002  = Used in MM:mm.loader.asm for RAM-based Memory Manager (obsolete, internal)B0B0  = Stolen by Claris for AWGS[end of document]